.TH DIRSWEEP 1 "November 2026" "dirsweep 4.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dirsweep \- remove empty and junk-only directories, with an undo
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dirsweep
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIPATH\fR...]
.br
.B dirsweep \-\-undo
.br
.B dirsweep \-\-restore
\fISESSION\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dirsweep
walks one or more directory trees and removes directories that are empty, or
that contain nothing but junk files (\fI.DS_Store\fR, \fIThumbs.db\fR, editor
swap and backup files, \fI*.log\fR, \fI*.tmp\fR and similar).
Chains of nested empty directories are removed in a single pass.
A directory that holds even one real file is left alone, junk included.
The target directory itself is never removed.
.PP
Symlinks are never followed (unless \fB\-\-follow\-symlinks\fR) and never
removed as directories. Other filesystems are not entered unless
\fB\-\-cross\-filesystems\fR is given.
.SH SELECTION
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-path " " \fIPATH\fR
Directory to clean. May be repeated; bare arguments are treated the same way.
Defaults to the current directory.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-subdirs
Only consider direct children of the target.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-max\-depth " " \fIN\fR
Consider at most N levels (0 = unlimited).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-strict\-empty
Remove only directories that are really empty; junk files count as content.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-exclude " " \fIREGEX\fR
Extended regular expression. A directory is skipped if its path relative to the
target, or any parent of that path, matches. Repeatable; commas separate
several patterns.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-junk " " \fIGLOB\fR
Additional junk file pattern. Patterns made only of wildcards are refused.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-default\-junk
Use only patterns given with \fB\-j\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-junk
Print the junk patterns in effect and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-min\-age \fIAGE\fR
Only touch directories whose modification time is at least AGE old. A bare
number means days; suffixes s, m, h, d, w are accepted.
Times are read before anything is deleted.
.SH SAFETY
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dry\-run
Report what would happen. The report matches a real run.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Ask before every removal: y, N, a (all), q (quit). Needs a terminal.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Skip the global confirmation. Without a terminal, dirsweep refuses to delete
unless this is given.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-trash
Record every removal so it can be undone. The record lives under
\fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/dirsweep/trash\fR (\fI/var/lib/dirsweep/trash\fR for root).
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-trash\-dir " " \fIDIR\fR
Like \fB\-\-trash\fR but keep the record in DIR, which must not be inside a target.
.TP
.B \-\-undo
Undo the most recent trash session.
.TP
.B \-\-restore \fISESSION\fR
Undo a specific session. Directories are recreated with their original mode,
owner (when permitted) and mtime; junk files are moved back. Nothing that
exists now is overwritten.
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Explain every decision.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print errors only.
.TP
.B \-\-progress
Show a progress bar on stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-json \fIFILE\fR
Write a JSON report (statistics, options, removed directories and files).
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-log " " \fIFILE\fR
Log file.
.TP
.B \-\-banner
Print the banner and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-banner
Do not print the banner at the start of a run. It is only shown on a terminal
in the first place.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable colors. \fBNO_COLOR\fR is honoured.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are read from \fI/etc/dirsweep.conf\fR, then
\fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dirsweep/config\fR (default \fI~/.config/dirsweep/config\fR),
then \fB\-C\fR \fIFILE\fR, then the command line. Files contain
\fIkey = value\fR lines and are never executed. See
\fI/usr/share/doc/dirsweep/examples\fR or the source repository for a sample.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Finished, but some removals failed (or nothing to undo).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error or refusal (protected path, no confirmation, bad option).
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/dirsweep/dirsweep.log
Default log (\fI/var/log/dirsweep.log\fR for root).
.SH LIMITATIONS
An empty directory that is the target of a symlink elsewhere is still removed,
leaving the link dangling. Paths with control characters other than newline,
carriage return and tab are not escaped in the JSON report. Linux with GNU
findutils and coreutils only.
.SH AUTHOR
Mohammad Sadra Naderi (ZVitoX), https://github.com/MS-X01
